  "prefLabel": "Env-A 2903.01 Legal Attributes of Allowances",
  "priorExpiration": "2011-11-09",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 2903.01 Legal Attributes of Allowances.\n\n(a) An allowance shall be a marketable emissions authorization that can be bought, sold, or traded at any time during any year, not just the current year.\n\n(b) An allowance shall not be a property right or create a property right for any person.\n\n(c) Future allocations shall not be a property right or create a property right for any person\n\n(d) No allowance or future allocation shall constitute a security or other form of property.\n\nSource. #7888, eff 5-13-03; ss by #9908, INTERIM, eff 5-13-11, EXPIRES: 11-9-11; ss by #10002, eff 10-1-11; ss by #12995, eff 2-25-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a2900.html"
